       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Chemical Peel Consent Form FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a chemical peel consent form?\", \"a\": \"A chemical peel consent form is the document a client reads and signs before a peel to record that she agrees to the treatment as your clinic describes it. For medical procedures, MedlinePlus describes written informed consent the same way: the patient reads a description of the treatment and signs a form. The description on your form comes from your provider, not from software.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a chemical peel consent form?\", \"a\": \"Describe the form in a prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>: your clinic, the peels you offer, the questions your provider asks, and where signed forms should go. Emergent builds the form and the table that stores each response, and you change either by prompting again. Paste your provider's approved wording rather than asking for new text.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I change in a chemical peel consent form template before clients sign it?\", \"a\": \"Change the wording first. A chemical peel consent form template was written for another clinic, and your provider or lawyer should replace its text with theirs. Then match its list of peels to your menu and its questions to the ones your provider asks. Starting from a chemical peel consent form PDF works too: paste its text into the prompt and edit from there.\"}, {\"q\": \"What makes a chemical peel consent form different from other service consents?\", \"a\": \"The shape is the same: approved wording, intake questions, and a signature. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/tattoo-consent'>tattoo consent form</a> follows that pattern too. What differs is what surrounds the signature at a peel clinic, such as a series of visits on one record or a check-in a few days later. Build those into the form when your clinic runs them, and leave them out when it does not.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I show different wording on a chemical peel consent form for each type of peel?\", \"a\": \"Add a question near the top that asks which peel is booked, and show only the section your provider wrote for that peel. A client booked for one peel never scrolls past wording meant for another. Your provider decides how many versions exist and what each one says.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a chemical peel consent form do after a yes answer?\", \"a\": \"The answer should reach your provider before the peel starts, and your provider decides what happens next. Have the app email that answer to whoever performs the peel, and pin it to the top of the client's record. Leave the decision itself out of the form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one visit cover a chemical peel consent form and another consent?\", \"a\": \"Yes: one link can open each treatment's consent in turn, each with its own wording and its own signature. A brow client who also books a peel could sign a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/permanent-makeup-consent'>permanent makeup consent form</a> and the peel consent in one sitting. Each signature saves as a separate record with its treatment named on it.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a client get a copy of the chemical peel consent form she signed?\", \"a\": \"Email it to her the moment she submits. Ask Emergent to add a button on the confirmation screen that sends the client a copy of her answers and signature. The record in your table holds the same answers and signature as the copy she receives.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I update a chemical peel consent form when the wording changes?\", \"a\": \"Paste the new wording into a prompt, and Emergent changes the form. Ask it to save a version number with each signature. A record signed last spring then still shows the wording that client saw, and it stays in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a chemical peel consent form live in the same app as my other service consents?\", \"a\": \"Yes: the app Emergent builds can hold a consent form for each service, all saving to client records in the same database. A spa that also waxes can add a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/waxing-consent'>waxing consent form</a> next to the peel consent. Staff then open either one from the client's record.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
