       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Class Registration Form FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a class registration form?\", \"a\": \"A class registration form is the form a student, or a parent for a child, fills in to take a seat in a specific class and section. It records who is taking the class and which section they chose, plus any contact or prerequisite details needed before the first session.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a class registration form?\", \"a\": \"Describe your classes and their seat limits in a prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the form and saves every sign-up to a database you own, and you change any rule later by asking in plain words. The free tier covers building and publishing.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a class registration form template include?\", \"a\": \"A class registration form template should include the student's full name and birth date, plus the class and section they want. Add contact details, with a guardian and an emergency contact for anyone under 18. Add prerequisite or skill-level questions only to the classes that need them. The same sections apply if you also keep a class registration form PDF at the front desk.\"}, {\"q\": \"How should a class registration form handle a class that runs for several weeks?\", \"a\": \"Register once for the whole run, not week by week. List the section with the dates of its first and last sessions and the day it meets. One sign-up then holds the seat for every session. If the program runs for whole days over the summer and families pick weeks, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/summer-camp-registration'>summer camp registration form</a> fits better.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a class registration form keep a waitlist for a full section?\", \"a\": \"Yes. When a section reaches its seat limit, the form offers a waitlist spot instead, and waitlisted students are saved in the order they joined. When someone drops, the app emails the first person on the list a link to claim the seat within a time you set, such as 48 hours. Emergent builds the waitlist and its emails from the same prompt as the form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a class registration form take payment at sign-up?\", \"a\": \"Take payment at sign-up when you want a seat to count only once it is paid. If an employer or a school pays later, collect the billing contact instead and mark the row unpaid. The app connects to your payment tool through its API, and each payment is recorded on the registrant's row.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one class registration form cover several classes at once?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Show the class list with the sections under each class, let the student pick as many as you allow, and save one row per class picked so every section's roster stays accurate. For a multi-day event with sessions and badges, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/conference-registration'>conference registration form</a> is the better fit.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I let students switch sections after they submit a class registration form?\", \"a\": \"Put a link to their own registration in the confirmation email. From it, a student picks a section with open seats; the app frees the old seat and emails both instructors. Set a cutoff, such as the day before the first session, after which changes go through staff. Emergent adds that change link when you ask for it in the prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a class registration form work in more than one language?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Write each question once per language and save every answer to the same field, and one table holds all sign-ups whatever language they came in. Have a fluent speaker check each translation before launch, and keep class names identical across versions to match rosters. Emergent builds both versions from one prompt and saves them to a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"What age details should a class registration form for kids collect?\", \"a\": \"Collect the birth date, not the age. A child who is 7 at sign-up may turn 8 before the class starts, and the birth date lets the form check eligibility against the first day of class. For ongoing childcare rather than a class with a set term, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/daycare-registration'>daycare registration form</a> collects the schedule and pickup details that care needs.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
